  "query_preview": "..\nIssued at 112 PM CST Tue Nov 3 2026\n\nA few light rain showers will continue to dissipate from west to \neast as the mid/upper trough continues to move northeast away from \nthe region. Large-scale forcing for subsidence is expected to bring \nclearing conditions this evening and tonight while breezy northwest \nwinds gradually diminish.\n\nThe next shortwave trough that is expected to arrive late Wed-\nThu is currently situated over northern California. This system \nis progged to race ESE into the Rockies on Wed before emerging \nover the Central Plains late Wed night into Thu. Seasonable \ntemperatures are anticipated ahead of this system with lows in \nthe upper 30s to mid 40s tonight, followed by a mild day on Wed \nwith plenty of insolation and light westerly winds helping to \nboost temperatures into the low to mid 60s. A compact shorwave \ntrough will arrive after midnght with increasing probabilities \nfor showers across southern KS through the day on Thu. This \nprogressive trough will move east of the area on Thursday \nevening with dry conditions returning.\n\nShortwave ridging is progged to build across the area on Fri \nbefore another progressive shortwave trough digs across the \nNorthern Plains ushering in some clouds and perhaps a few \nsprinkles on Sat, although most locations should remain dry. \nSeasonble temperatures are anticipated through the weekend with \nhighs in the 60s.\n\nA mid/upper ridge is progged to build over the central CONUS late in \nthe weekend into early next week bringing rising heights/increasing \nthickness and rising temperatures. Above average temperatures are \nexpected to prevail with dry weather condtions anticipated.",
